-| `media/settings.{js,css}` | Shared settings surface — a view over existing gear prefs/actions plus the voice send-phrase / dictionary setters. Nav order General → Voice → Notifications → Providers → Connectors → Account → Advanced → About (Chat is folded into General; each nav row is icon + label). Connectors is gated on `capabilities.mcpSettings` (OPT-IN: absent/false = hide the nav row; desktop and VS Code set true) and has three sections: On this computer (host-owned Tier-1 list — Connect / Disconnect on the desk and on remotes when `mcpConnectors.remoteConnect` is present; key-auth rows paste a token in-row and never render it back; remote OAuth opens consent on the requesting device and completes automatically through the relay callback; older hosts offer no remote controls; disconnect copy says running sessions retain their tools; `sortConnectorsForDisplay` is connected-first then name, case-insensitive; vendor marks from `media/connector-logos/<id>.webp` on those rows only, hidden until load and removed on error), Grok.com connectors (account-level, Grok only — Open grok.com in the section header; `scopeName` is the team name), and Local Grok connectors (this machine's Grok config files — header Open posts `openGlobalConfig` on the desk even when the section is empty, lucide `settings` gear (`ICON_SETTINGS`); remote gets a sentence, not a disabled button). Project-file servers are omitted. Origin tags are gone. General order is purpose → text size → coding display toggles → steer → usage stats → thumbs. Providers nav uses a bot icon; Connectors uses the plug. About carries versions, the host-gated CLI update action, Report a bug / Request a feature (GitHub tracker), contact `mailto:support@productcompass.pm`, and the non-affiliation disclaimer as the last element on that page only. The gear has no Version & about entry. Desktop/remote open the in-page overlay from gear → **Settings**; VS Code opens an editor-area tab (`grok.settings` + view/title gear). Overlay clients get a top-left **← Back to app** link above search (Escape-equivalent, focus returns to the opener, inside the Tab trap); the VS Code tab does not. Remote keeps host-owned settings and connection status, the device-manager link, the live Grok inventory, and the grok.com link; Advanced host-local rows stay hidden. Tier-1 connector management uses the capability gate described above. Overlay is keyboard-contained (Tab trap + sibling `inert`/`aria-hidden`, focus restored after `paint`, Escape or Back to app returns to the opener). `update()` is a no-op when the displayed snapshot/env is unchanged (`paintKey`); a host-driven change while the phone category `<select>` is open (`describeChrome.navMenuOpen`) defers `paint` until that control blurs, so a live frame cannot close the native picker. Restore defaults only resets toggles/selects/sliders (`restoreTargets` / `restoreChanges` — never send phrase or dictionary terms); a page with nothing restorable has no button, and the action first expands an in-surface confirm listing the rows that will change. Snapshot-on-open for the tab; changes post the same `set*`/`open*` messages plus `setVoiceSendPhrase` / `setVoiceKeyterms` / `setTelemetryEnabled` / `setThumbsFeedback`. General includes *Thumbs feedback to SpaceXAI* (`grok.thumbsFeedback`, default off) as a desk toggle and a remote read-only status (same split as Anonymous usage stats — the phone cannot write a privacy setting the policy rejects). Grok.com connector rows show `scopeName` when the CLI sends a team name |
